   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_call240_rrtm_lw_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NLAYERS = 103, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF@592f693 (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and inside SUBROUTINE RRTM/RTRN, dump scm_cloud_240.json, tile column 0; written by the same em_scm_xy run re-executed for 8 h with the cloudy calls added to ESM_DUMP_CALLS, which reproduces the archived call 120 dump bit-for-bit). RRTM has no standalone driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. This document runs the WHOLE longwave chain from the WRF column state: RRTMColumn (MM5ATM) -> RRTMSetcoef -> RRTMGasOptics (TAUGB1-16 + GASABS) -> RTRNSweep -> RRTMLWHeating, each stage fed by the previous one through variable_map/param_to_var edges into the stages' `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters (the mount-edge libraries lower the `input_<x>` rewrite targets to those parameters); only the column state (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, q*, cldfra, dz8w, pi3d), the surface scalars (tsk, emiss, co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr) and WRF's zero cross-section columns are prescribed. Tolerances are END-TO-END, wider than the stages' own because the sweep now consumes the gas optics' quantised ITR (exact up to +/-1 flips of the 1/5000 transition-fraction index; rrtm_gas_optics.esm) instead of the dumped ITR, and each flip perturbs one g-point optical depth: fluxes Linf abs 5e-3 W/m^2 (measured TOLFLUX at this call) and spot checks / glw / olr rel 2e-5 (measured TOLREL), HTR Linf abs 5e-3 K/day (measured TOLHTR) and spot checks rel 2e-4 at the three cloudy layers 51, 52 and the fractional layer 55 (measured TOLHTRSPOT; HTR is a real32 difference of O(300 W/m^2) fluxes over O(6 hPa), and these three |HTR| are only 0.6-1.0 K/day, hence 2e-4 rather than the 1e-4 used where |HTR| is large), dTdt/dthdt Linf abs 2e-8 K/s (measured TOLDT). The column-setup identities (col_tz, col_tavel, col_tbound) keep the stage tolerances. The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: CLOUD OVERLAP WITH FRACTIONAL CLOUD -- call 240 (21:00 UTC, 14:34 LST), the decaying cirrus deck. MM5ATM overrides CLDFRA 0.0542, 0.355, 0.402, 0.388 to CLDFRAC = 1 in RRTM layers 51-54 because their TAUCLOUD (0.0728, 0.1423, 0.0709, 0.0403) exceeds 0.01, while layer 55 keeps its diagnosed CLDFRA = 0.1470 at TAUCLOUD = 0.009966 -- the largest fractional cloud fraction the scheme admits in this run -- so the RTRN sweeps run the fractional-cloud branch (EFCLFRAC = ABSCLD CLDFRAC = 0.00241 against ABSCLD = 0.01641) end-to-end from the WRF column state. Surface cloud forcing 13.8 W/m^2.",
